<% layout("/layouts/boilerplate") %>

<div class="container-xl">
  <article class="legal">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: <%= lastUpdated %></p>
    <p>
      These terms govern your use of Travel Roots. By creating an account, publishing a listing or booking a stay
      you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use the service.
    </p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#accounts">Accounts</a></li>
        <li><a href="#role">Our role</a></li>
        <li><a href="#hosts">Host responsibilities</a></li>
        <li><a href="#guests">Guest responsibilities</a></li>
        <li><a href="#payments">Bookings and payments</a></li>
        <li><a href="#content">Reviews and content</a></li>
        <li><a href="#conduct">Prohibited conduct</a></li>
        <li><a href="#termination">Suspension and termination</a></li>
        <li><a href="#liability">Disclaimers and liability</a></li>
        <li><a href="#general">General</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="accounts">1. Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 18 years old to use Travel Roots. Provide accurate information, keep your password
      confidential and let us know straight away if you think your account has been used without permission. You
      are responsible for activity on your account.
    </p>

    <h2 id="role">2. Our role</h2>
    <p>
      Travel Roots is a platform that connects hosts who offer stays with guests who want to book them. Hosts are
      responsible for their listings and for providing the stay. We are not the owner or operator of any listed
      property.
    </p>

    <h2 id="hosts">3. Host responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Only list places you own or are authorised to rent out.</li>
      <li>Describe your place accurately, use your own photos and keep prices and contact details up to date.</li>
      <li>Comply with local laws, permits, safety requirements and tax obligations that apply to short-term stays.</li>
      <li>Honour confirmed bookings and respond to guests promptly.</li>
      <li>A listing with upcoming confirmed stays cannot be deleted until those stays are complete.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="guests">4. Guest responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Treat the property and neighbours with respect and follow the host's house rules.</li>
      <li>Use the place only for the dates and purpose you booked.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for damage caused during your stay.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="payments">5. Bookings and payments</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Prices are shown per night in Indian Rupees. GST at <%= Math.round(taxRate * 100) %>% is added to the accommodation total at checkout.</li>
      <li>Payments are processed by Razorpay. A booking is confirmed only after the payment has been verified by our servers.</li>
      <li>Stays can be booked for up to 30 nights and up to 365 days in advance. Dates that overlap an existing confirmed booking cannot be booked.</li>
      <li>Cancellations, changes and refunds are agreed between the guest and the host. Use the host contact details on your booking to arrange them.</li>
      <li>If you were charged but did not receive a confirmation, contact <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> with your booking reference.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="content">6. Reviews and content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of the content you post, such as listings, photos and reviews. By posting it you give
      Travel Roots a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to host, display and adapt it for the purpose of operating
      and promoting the service. Reviews must reflect a genuine experience. We may remove content that breaks these
      terms or the law.
    </p>

    <h2 id="conduct">7. Prohibited conduct</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Posting false, misleading, discriminatory, abusive or illegal content.</li>
      <li>Attempting to take payments outside the platform in a way that misleads other users.</li>
      <li>Interfering with the service, probing for vulnerabilities without permission, scraping or automated abuse.</li>
      <li>Using another person's account or identity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="termination">8. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time from Account settings. We may suspend or close accounts that break
      these terms or put other users at risk. Terms that by their nature should survive, such as payment
      obligations and limitations of liability, continue after termination.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">9. Disclaimers and liability</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided "as is". We work to keep it available and accurate but do not guarantee that it will
      be uninterrupted or error-free, or that listings are accurate. To the extent permitted by law, Travel Roots is
      not liable for indirect or consequential losses, and our total liability for any claim is limited to the fees
      you paid through the platform for the booking concerned. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot
      be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2 id="general">10. General</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of India. We may update them from time to time; if a change is
      significant we will give notice on the website. Continued use after a change means you accept the updated
      terms. Questions can be sent to <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</div>
